window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"yasuo","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Yasuo","Yasuo","Skill","Skill","Yasuo","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Steel Tempest's 475 reach against The Darkin Glaive (10s at rank 1), a melee empowered attack, lets you dictate - dash circles around him."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"His Q and Aureate Rush (E, 10s at rank 1) mature - the dash deals max-health damage, so do not eat it with your shield down; trade off his cooldowns."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"If he holds Grim Deliverance (R, 110s at rank 1) for your knockup all-in, the fight evens - bait it with an E-Q flurry you can walk out of, then commit Last Breath."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your crit spike plus flow shield wins the duel again - force fights before his second item closes the window."}],"wants":{"you":["Range answers on his melee glaive combo","Dash tempo he cannot pin down","His R baited before the real knockup all-in"],"foe":["Q Darkin Glaive chip through wall gaps","Aureate Rush (E) catching your dash-in","Grim Deliverance healing him through your all-in"]},"early":"Level 1 is a farm-off with no committed all-in from either side, then you take charge: at 2 Steel Tempest's 475 range beats The Darkin Glaive, a melee empowered attack he must walk in for, and by 3 your E mobility controls the trade tempo completely - he only touches you when you err.","mid":"Levels 4-5 even out as both kits live on cooldowns - respect Aureate Rush (E, 10s), whose max-health damage armour will not answer, when your shield is down. Level 6 is a mind game: your knockup-into-Last Breath beats him, but Grim Deliverance heals him out of it, so drain the 110s with a fake engage first.","late":"First item restores your edge - crit spike plus flow shield out-trades his bruiser rotation - and two items in you stay ahead as the roaming pick threat: Wind Wall wins every extended duel by deleting half his damage, and your mobility means he never chooses when the fight starts. Snowball the map.","whys":["Level 1 is even - both of you farm with no committed all-in.","You own level 2 — Steel Tempest at 475 range outranges his melee Q.","At 3 your E dash tempo controls the trade — he must commit first.","Levels 4-5 even out as he stabilises farm and you both play cooldowns.","Level 6 is even - his R, Grim Deliverance, heals him through your knockup all-in.","First item is yours: the crit spike and shield passive out-trade him.","Two items in your mobility and Wind Wall keep you ahead as the pick threat."]});
